# K1: Codex findings whose quoted ranges are not co-located with any primary/replica record (never in a multi-run region).
# Each is normalized to the claim it attributes to the quoted text; all remain singletons (NO_CO_LOCATED_RECORD_FROM_OTHER_RUN).
# These findings describe checker/hook implementation behavior; their original labels (AMBIGUOUS / POTENTIAL_EXTRA) stay attributed provenance only.
CX X:BF-K1-0120 | The manifest checker parses project files textually (Include references, raw attributes) without evaluating MSBuild conditions, properties or imports (reported uncertainty).
CX X:BF-K1-0125 | Per-file manifest-checker arguments must resolve inside the active root; warnings alone yield success and missing selected files return no findings (reported uncertainty).
CX X:BF-K1-0129 | The command classifier inspects shell wrappers only when they carry recognized inline commands; script-file execution is not inspected before it runs (reported uncertainty).
CX X:BF-K1-0137 | Active-root resolution prefers worktree/enclosing instruction roots, and the CLI can fall back to the script root when the cwd lacks .claude (reported uncertainty).
CX X:BF-K1-0138 | Checker text decoding rejects NUL-containing non-BOM input, and file walks skip named build/tool directories and nested Git roots.
CX X:BF-K1-0139 | The checker XML reader is a minimal textual parser requiring quoted attributes, not an evaluated MSBuild graph or a complete XML validator (reported uncertainty).
CX X:BF-K1-0141 | Actual-state enforcement uses a 5000-entry limit and selected manifest, input and instruction paths, excluding ignored directories and settings.local.json.
CX X:BF-K1-0142 | The actual-state checker persists a per-worktree snapshot, or a lowercased-root temporary-file snapshot outside Git, and re-baselines automatically on unreadable state (reported uncertainty).
CX X:BF-K1-0144 | Actual-state attribution is limited by first-observation and moved-HEAD baselines; overflow reverts to dirty-file checks and there is no initial non-Git reference baseline (reported uncertainty).
CX X:BF-K1-0147 | Co-change hook reminders are deduplicated by triggering-path content with the latest 100 fingerprints; the CLI always reports and non-Git trees are skipped.
CX X:BF-K1-0191 | When the hook payload lacks cwd, dispatch falls back to process.cwd, so the repository checked may depend on the launcher environment (reported uncertainty).
CX X:BF-K1-0193 | Post-tool checks depend on a fixed shell/edit tool set and in-root path resolution; failed shell commands are inspected for changes too (reported uncertainty).
